  "query_preview": "..\n\nGenerally uneventful weather pattern in the extended portion of the \nforecast, wrapping up October neatly. A ridge of high pressure in \nthe Gulf will be the main feature driving the weather in SE AK. \nOffshore flow will lead to milder weather and limited to no \nprecipitation for much of this week. Early in the week, the feature \nmost worthy of discussing is a small low which intensifies a bit \nover the southern panhandle and move further south. This will amp up \nthe N-S pressure gradient on Tuesday into Wednesday, increasing \nnortherly winds in Lynn Canal, and potentially other N-S inner \nchannels to a lesser extent.\n\nLater in the week on Friday the next considerable low and attendant \nfronts will be moving into the Gulf, raising rain chances yet\nagain.",
